{
  "_README": [
    "Editorial layer over the raw ontology (ontology_source/). Everything here is a",
    "human decision that cannot be derived from the source data. Edit freely and re-run:",
    "    python Backend/tree_data/build_from_ontology.py --out-dir Backend/tree_data --force",
    "",
    "topic_aliases : raw topic_code -> canonical topic_code. The source ontology was",
    "  assembled from three drafts, so the same topic appears under 2-3 codes",
    "  (MAT_ vs MATH_, CHE_ vs CHEM_, PHY_GRAV vs PHY_GRAVITATION). Unmerged, the",
    "  catalog lists a topic twice and topic practice only ever covers half of it.",
    "topic_labels  : canonical topic_code -> display label (leading syllabus numbers stripped).",
    "courses       : one course per subject; sections group canonical topics into",
    "  syllabus areas. Section order is the intended study order.",
    "",
    "Any canonical topic not listed under a section is still ingested, but will not",
    "appear in the catalog. The build reports those."
  ],

